  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset market in late August 2026 is defined by the upcoming September 15th Senate cloture vote on the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act (H.R. 3633), representing a critical regulatory threshold for U.S. market structure. Institutional Bitcoin participation has matured from initial spot ETF accumulation into structured, long-term corporate treasury reserve management and pension fund allocation. Concurrently, regulatory momentum is accelerating interest in high-assurance, deterministic Bitcoin-native smart contract execution as a structural competitor to Ethereum's dominant EVM ecosystem. In parallel, cross-chain infrastructure is rapidly transitioning from vulnerable custodial bridges toward non-custodial atomic routing and unified liquidity aggregators bridging Bitcoin and Ethereum.",
